@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Desktop changed-field editing and review integrity
hide footbox
autonumber
actor Maintainer
participant "app : App" as App
participant "dataset\n<<module>>" as Dataset
activate Maintainer
Maintainer -> App : _save_browse_edit()
activate App
alt No selected ID / blank edited expression
  note over App : Explain required selection/text; do not write.
else Valid selected draft
  note over App : Diff editable values against the selected snapshot.\nPreserve unchanged legacy whitespace and metadata.\nApproval is valid only for the exact reviewed values.
  App -> Dataset : update_entry(selected_id, changed_fields)
  activate Dataset
  note over Dataset : Under one reentrant lock: load, find ID, apply update,\natomically replace CSV; never rewrite a missing ID.
  Dataset --> App : Commit / EntryNotFoundError / storage failure
  deactivate Dataset
  alt Missing ID or write failure
    note over App : Preserve edits; report failure, never Changes saved.
  else Commit succeeded
    App -> App : apply committed values to local snapshot
    activate App
    App --> App : Snapshot/review state synchronized
    deactivate App
    App -> Dataset : load_all() through _refresh_views()
    activate Dataset
    Dataset --> App : Shared snapshot or refresh failure
    deactivate Dataset
    note over App : Repopulate from the fresh cached row if present.\nReport committed save separately from a failed refresh\nor a row removed after the transaction.
  end
end
App --> Maintainer : Saved or recoverable editor state
deactivate App
deactivate Maintainer
legend bottom
  Desktop edits preserve ID, timestamp, contributor and audio reference.
  Text, glosses, topic, location, notes, language and lexical metadata are editable.
  Locks prevent interleaved writes, not semantic last-writer-wins conflicts.
endlegend
@enduml
